  "body": "All the spec seems to say on the matter right now is this:\r\n\r\n> The user agent should allow the user to manually trigger elements that have an activation behavior, for instance using keyboard or voice input, or through mouse clicks. When the user triggers an element with a defined activation behavior in a manner other than clicking it, the default action of the interaction event must be to fire a click event at the element.\r\n\r\nBut in practice, it's pretty much universal that enter and space trigger activation behavior for buttons (both `<input>` and `<button>`), as far as I can tell, so that should be mentioned, at least in a note.\r\n\r\nAnd UAs aren't even consistent there.  Some of them put the button in :active state for space being pressed, but none of them seem to put it in :active state for enter being pressed...",
